/-!
# Derived localization away from one element, in a free module universe

Let `A` be a commutative ring in `Type u` and let `f ∈ A`. The endofunctor
`Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locFunctor f` of `A`-modules is extension of scalars to
`Localization.Away f` followed by restriction of scalars; since `Localization.Away f` lives in
`Type u`, the tensor product `A[1/f] ⊗[A] M` lives in `Type (max u v)` even when `M` lives in
`Type v`, and `locFunctor` is therefore an endofunctor of `ModuleCat.{max v u} A` and not of
`ModuleCat.{v} A`. The same is true of its derived companion `locDerived`, and hence of the
orthogonality statement `Stacks.LocalCohomology.subsingleton_hom_singleFunctor_directSum`
which makes the extended alternating Čech complex a coreflection.

This file removes the constraint. The localizing submonoid is `Submonoid.powers f`, generated by
a single element and hence a quotient of `ℕ`, so `LocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers f) M` is
`Small.{w}` whenever `M` is — in particular for *every* `M : ModuleCat.{w} A`, with no relation
between `w` and `u` and no smallness hypothesis on `A`. Replacing `A[1/f] ⊗[A] M` by the
canonical `Shrink` model of `LocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers f) M` gives
`Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locFunctorShrink`, an endofunctor of `ModuleCat.{w} A` for a
module universe `w` independent of the ring universe `u`, together with
`Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locDerivedShrink` on `D(A)`.

Unlike the Čech comparison of `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.Shrink`, nothing here is a transport
across a degreewise equivalence: `locFunctorShrink` is *the* localization functor, characterised
by `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.isLocalizedModule_locUnitShrink`. It is the specialisation
to `Submonoid.powers f` of the localization functor at an arbitrary `Small.{w}` submonoid in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.TorsionComplete.SmallLocalization`, from which everything about
it is inherited rather than reproved; what this file adds is the comparison with the pinned
functors of `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.Ext` and the orthogonality of an `f`-local module
to an `f`-torsion object, ending where the small Čech complex and the small localization meet.

## Main definitions

* `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locModShrink`,
  `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locMkShrink` — the `w`-small model of `M[1/f]` and the
  localization map into it.
* `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locFunctorShrink`,
  `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locUnitShrink` — **localization away from `f` as an
  endofunctor of `ModuleCat.{w} A` for `w` independent of the ring universe**, and its unit.
* `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locDerivedShrink`,
  `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locDerivedUnitShrink` — **the same on `D(A)`**.

## Main results

* `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.isLocalizedModule_locUnitShrink` — the unit exhibits
  `locFunctorShrink` as localization at the powers of `f`; this is the characterisation the
  general development is proved from.
* `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locFunctorShrink_isZero_iff` — the localization vanishes
  exactly when every element is killed by a power of `f`, which is the shape
  `Dualizing.isZero_smallLocalization_iff` takes at `Submonoid.powers f`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.subsingleton_hom_singleFunctorShrink_of_isUnit_smul`,
  `Stacks.LocalCohomology.subsingleton_hom_singleFunctorShrink_directSum` — **a module on which
  `f` acts invertibly, placed in any degree, receives no nonzero morphism from an object killed
  by the derived localization at `f`**, in a module universe independent of the ring universe.
* `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locFunctorShrinkIso`,
  `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locDerivedShrinkIso` — at the pinned universe the free
  construction is canonically isomorphic to `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locFunctor` and to
  `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locDerived`; so this is a generalisation of those functors
  and not a second notion of localization.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.subsingleton_hom_singleFunctorShrink_extendedCechComplexShrink_X` —
  **the Čech terms away from degree zero are invisible to torsion objects, in a module universe
  independent of the ring universe.** This is where the small Čech complex of
  `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.Shrink` and the small localization functor meet: the statement
  needs both, which is why it is pinned at `ModuleCat.{max u v}` in
  `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.CechModel` even though neither ingredient has to be.

## Implementation notes

`Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Localization` has the localization functor
`ModuleCat.localizedModuleFunctor` at an arbitrary submonoid, but it assumes `Small.{w} A`,
which for an arbitrary submonoid is exactly what is needed. At the powers of a single element
that hypothesis is unnecessary, and dropping it is what makes the module universe here
genuinely free.

The construction at an arbitrary `Small.{w}` submonoid lives in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.TorsionComplete.SmallLocalization` as
`Dualizing.smallLocalization`, `Dualizing.smallLocalizationMk`,
`Dualizing.smallLocalizationFunctor` and `Dualizing.smallLocalizationUnit`, with
`Dualizing.small_submonoidPowers` supplying the smallness hypothesis at `Submonoid.powers f`.
Beware that `Dualizing.smallLocalizationUnit` is the natural transformation
`𝟭 ⟶ smallLocalizationFunctor S` while `Dualizing.smallLocalizationMk` is its underlying linear
map; `locUnitShrink` is the former and `locMkShrink` the latter. The names below are that
construction's specialisation, placed in the namespace of the functor they generalise; every one
of them is it definitionally, so the vanishing, idempotence, exactness and power-torsion
statements are inherited from the general development and not proved again here.

The small model is kept behind `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locModShrink`, a definition
typed at `ModuleCat.{w} A`, rather than used as a bare `Shrink`: the scalar-tower instances that
`Module.End` and `algebraMap` require are not available on `Shrink` itself, and are read off the
`ModuleCat` object instead.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A6R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A6R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DWR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DWR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05EH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05EH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe w v u w'

namespace Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

section Localizations

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- The `w`-small model of the localization `M[1/f]`, as an object of `ModuleCat.{w} A`: the
localization of `M` at `Submonoid.powers f`, which is available in the module universe of `M`
alone because the powers of a single element are a quotient of `ℕ`. -/
@[ega "I 1.3.1"]
def locModShrink (f : A) (M : ModuleCat.{w} A) : ModuleCat.{w} A :=
  Dualizing.smallLocalization (Submonoid.powers f) M

/-- The localization map `M ⟶ M[1/f]` into the small model. -/
def locMkShrink (f : A) (M : ModuleCat.{w} A) : M →ₗ[A] locModShrink.{w} f M :=
  Dualizing.smallLocalizationMk (Submonoid.powers f) M

/-- The map `locMkShrink f M : M → M[1/f]` is a localization of `M` at the powers of `f`. -/
instance isLocalizedModule_locMkShrink (f : A) (M : ModuleCat.{w} A) :
    IsLocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers f) (locMkShrink.{w} f M) :=
  Dualizing.isLocalizedModule_smallLocalizationMk (Submonoid.powers f) M

/-- **Localization away from `f`, as an endofunctor of `ModuleCat.{w} A` for a module universe
`w` independent of the ring universe.** It is localization at the submonoid `Submonoid.powers f`,
which is `Small.{w}` for every `w`. -/
def locFunctorShrink (f : A) : ModuleCat.{w} A ⥤ ModuleCat.{w} A :=
  Dualizing.smallLocalizationFunctor (Submonoid.powers f)

/-- The localization maps `M ⟶ M[1/f]`, as a natural transformation out of the identity. -/
def locUnitShrink (f : A) : 𝟭 (ModuleCat.{w} A) ⟶ locFunctorShrink.{w} f :=
  Dualizing.smallLocalizationUnit (Submonoid.powers f)

/-- **The unit exhibits `M[1/f]` as the localization of `M` at the powers of `f`.** -/
lemma isLocalizedModule_locUnitShrink (f : A) (M : ModuleCat.{w} A) :
    IsLocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers f) ((locUnitShrink.{w} f).app M).hom :=
  isLocalizedModule_locMkShrink.{w} f M

/-- Localization away from `f` is additive. -/
instance locFunctorShrink_additive (f : A) : (locFunctorShrink.{w} f).Additive :=
  Dualizing.smallLocalizationFunctor_additive (Submonoid.powers f)

/-- Localization away from `f` is left exact. -/
instance locFunctorShrink_preservesFiniteLimits (f : A) :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (locFunctorShrink.{w} f) :=
  Dualizing.smallLocalizationFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits (Submonoid.powers f)

/-- Localization away from `f` is right exact. -/
instance locFunctorShrink_preservesFiniteColimits (f : A) :
    PreservesFiniteColimits (locFunctorShrink.{w} f) :=
  Dualizing.smallLocalizationFunctor_preservesFiniteColimits (Submonoid.powers f)

/-- `f` acts invertibly on `M[1/f]`. -/
lemma isUnit_algebraMap_locFunctorShrink (f : A) (M : ModuleCat.{w} A) :
    IsUnit (algebraMap A (Module.End A ((locFunctorShrink.{w} f).obj M)) f) :=
  IsLocalizedModule.map_units (locMkShrink.{w} f M) ⟨f, Submonoid.mem_powers f⟩

/-- If `f` acts invertibly on `N`, then `N ⟶ N[1/f]` is an isomorphism. -/
lemma isIso_locUnitShrink_of_isUnit (f : A) (N : ModuleCat.{w} A)
    (h : IsUnit (algebraMap A (Module.End A N) f)) : IsIso ((locUnitShrink.{w} f).app N) := by
  have hu : ∀ s : Submonoid.powers f, IsUnit (algebraMap A (Module.End A N) (s : A)) := by
    rintro ⟨s, n, rfl⟩
    simpa only [map_pow] using h.pow n
  exact (ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective _).2
    (Dualizing.bijective_smallLocalizationMk (Submonoid.powers f) N hu)

/-- `M[1/f]` vanishes exactly when every element of `M` is killed by a power of `f`. This is
`Dualizing.isZero_smallLocalization_iff` with the submonoid unpacked as the powers of `f`. -/
lemma locFunctorShrink_isZero_iff (f : A) (M : ModuleCat.{w} A) :
    IsZero ((locFunctorShrink.{w} f).obj M) ↔ ∀ m : M, ∃ n : ℕ, f ^ n • m = 0 :=
  (Dualizing.isZero_smallLocalization_iff (Submonoid.powers f) M).trans
    ⟨fun h m => by obtain ⟨⟨_, n, rfl⟩, hr⟩ := h m; exact ⟨n, hr⟩,
      fun h m => by obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := h m; exact ⟨⟨f ^ n, n, rfl⟩, hn⟩⟩

end Localizations

/-! ### Derived localization in a free module universe -/

section DerivedLocalization

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- **Derived localization away from `f`, as an endofunctor of `D(A)` for a module universe
independent of the ring universe.** -/
def locDerivedShrink (f : A) :
    DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{w} A) ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{w} A) :=
  (locFunctorShrink.{w} f).mapDerivedCategory

/-- The derived localization maps, as a natural transformation out of the identity. -/
def locDerivedUnitShrink (f : A) :
    𝟭 (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{w} A)) ⟶ locDerivedShrink.{w} f :=
  Coreflection.derivedUnit (locFunctorShrink.{w} f) (locUnitShrink.{w} f)

/-- Derived localization is additive. -/
instance locDerivedShrink_additive (f : A) : (locDerivedShrink.{w} f).Additive :=
  inferInstanceAs ((locFunctorShrink.{w} f).mapDerivedCategory.Additive)

/-- Derived localization commutes with the shift. -/
instance locDerivedShrink_commShift (f : A) : (locDerivedShrink.{w} f).CommShift ℤ :=
  inferInstanceAs ((locFunctorShrink.{w} f).mapDerivedCategory.CommShift ℤ)

/-- Derived localization is triangulated. -/
instance locDerivedShrink_isTriangulated (f : A) : (locDerivedShrink.{w} f).IsTriangulated :=
  inferInstanceAs ((locFunctorShrink.{w} f).mapDerivedCategory.IsTriangulated)

/-- Derived localization is idempotent: the unit is invertible on its image. -/
lemma isIso_locDerivedUnitShrink_locDerivedShrink (f : A)
    (X : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{w} A)) :
    IsIso ((locDerivedUnitShrink.{w} f).app ((locDerivedShrink.{w} f).obj X)) :=
  Coreflection.derivedUnit_obj_isIso (locFunctorShrink.{w} f) (locUnitShrink.{w} f)
    (fun M => Dualizing.isIso_smallLocalizationUnit_app_obj (Submonoid.powers f) M) X

/-- Derived localization inverts its own unit. -/
lemma isIso_locDerivedShrink_map_locDerivedUnitShrink (f : A)
    (X : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{w} A)) :
    IsIso ((locDerivedShrink.{w} f).map ((locDerivedUnitShrink.{w} f).app X)) :=
  Coreflection.derivedUnit_map_isIso (locFunctorShrink.{w} f) (locUnitShrink.{w} f)
    (fun M => Dualizing.isIso_smallLocalizationFunctor_map_smallLocalizationUnit_app
      (Submonoid.powers f) M) X

end DerivedLocalization

/-! ### Comparison with the localization functor of `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.Ext`

At the pinned universe `max v u` the two constructions agree: both are localization of the
module at the powers of `f`, so they are canonically isomorphic, naturally in the module and
compatibly with the two units. The free-universe functor is therefore a *generalisation* of
`Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locFunctor` and not a second notion of localization. -/

section Comparison

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- **The small model agrees with the localization functor of
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Dualizing.Ext` at the pinned universe**, naturally in the module: both
exhibit the module's localization at the powers of `f`. -/
def locFunctorShrinkIso (f : A) : locFunctorShrink.{max v u} f ≅ locFunctor.{v} f := by
  letI inst (M : ModuleCat.{max v u} A) :
      IsLocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers f) ((locUnit.{v} f).app M).hom :=
    isLocalizedModule_locUnit f M
  refine NatIso.ofComponents (fun M =>
    (IsLocalizedModule.linearEquiv (Submonoid.powers f)
      (locMkShrink.{max v u} f M) ((locUnit.{v} f).app M).hom).toModuleIso) ?_
  intro M N φ
  apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
  apply IsLocalizedModule.ext (Submonoid.powers f) (locMkShrink.{max v u} f M)
    (IsLocalizedModule.map_units ((locUnit.{v} f).app N).hom)
  ext x
  change (IsLocalizedModule.linearEquiv (Submonoid.powers f)
      (locMkShrink.{max v u} f N) ((locUnit.{v} f).app N).hom)
        ((IsLocalizedModule.map (Submonoid.powers f) (locMkShrink.{max v u} f M)
          (locMkShrink.{max v u} f N) φ.hom) (locMkShrink.{max v u} f M x)) =
    ((locFunctor.{v} f).map φ).hom
      ((IsLocalizedModule.linearEquiv (Submonoid.powers f) (locMkShrink.{max v u} f M)
        ((locUnit.{v} f).app M).hom) (locMkShrink.{max v u} f M x))
  rw [IsLocalizedModule.map_apply, IsLocalizedModule.linearEquiv_apply,
    IsLocalizedModule.linearEquiv_apply]
  exact congrFun (congrArg DFunLike.coe
    (congrArg ModuleCat.Hom.hom ((locUnit.{v} f).naturality φ).symm)) x

/-- The comparison carries the unit of the small model to the unit of
`Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locFunctor`. -/
lemma locUnitShrink_comp_locFunctorShrinkIso (f : A) (M : ModuleCat.{max v u} A) :
    (locUnitShrink.{max v u} f).app M ≫ (locFunctorShrinkIso f).hom.app M
      = (locUnit.{v} f).app M := by
  have : IsLocalizedModule (Submonoid.powers f) ((locUnit.{v} f).app M).hom :=
    isLocalizedModule_locUnit f M
  apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
  ext x
  exact IsLocalizedModule.linearEquiv_apply (Submonoid.powers f)
    (locMkShrink.{max v u} f M) ((locUnit.{v} f).app M).hom x

/-- **The derived small model agrees with `Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange.locDerived` at the
pinned universe.** -/
def locDerivedShrinkIso (f : A) : locDerivedShrink.{max v u} f ≅ locDerived.{v} f :=
  Stacks.DerivedCategoryComparisons.mapDerivedCategoryIsoOfNatIso _ _ (locFunctorShrinkIso f)

/-- The hypothesis of `Stacks.LocalCohomology.subsingleton_hom_singleFunctor_directSum` may be
checked with either functor: at the pinned universe the two derived localizations vanish
together. -/
lemma locDerivedShrink_isZero_iff_locDerived_isZero (f : A)
    (X : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{max v u} A)) :
    IsZero ((locDerivedShrink.{max v u} f).obj X) ↔ IsZero ((locDerived.{v} f).obj X) :=
  ((locDerivedShrinkIso f).app X).isZero_iff

end Comparison

end Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange

/-! ### Orthogonality of a local module to a torsion object, at a free module universe -/

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

open Dualizing.PowerTorsionBaseChange

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-- **Orthogonality of a local module to a torsion object, in a module universe independent of
the ring universe.** If `g` acts invertibly on the `A`-module `N` and the derived localization of
`W` at `g` vanishes, then every morphism from `W` to `N` placed in degree `q` is zero. This is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.subsingleton_hom_singleFunctor_of_isUnit_smul` with the constraint
`ModuleCat.{max v u}` removed. -/
theorem subsingleton_hom_singleFunctorShrink_of_isUnit_smul (g : A)
    (W : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{w} A)) (hW : IsZero ((locDerivedShrink.{w} g).obj W))
    (N : ModuleCat.{w} A) (hN : IsUnit (algebraMap A (Module.End A N) g)) (q : ℤ) :
    Subsingleton (W ⟶ (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} A) q).obj N) := by
  have hloc : IsIso ((locDerivedUnitShrink.{w} g).app
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} A) q).obj N)) :=
    isIso_derivedUnit_app_singleFunctor (locFunctorShrink.{w} g) (locUnitShrink.{w} g) N q
      (isIso_locUnitShrink_of_isUnit.{w} g N hN)
  exact subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun u =>
    hom_eq_zero_of_isLocal (locDerivedShrink.{w} g) (locDerivedUnitShrink.{w} g) hW hloc u

/-- The same conclusion for a finite direct sum of modules, each carrying its own element acting
invertibly on it, in a module universe independent of the ring universe. -/
theorem subsingleton_hom_singleFunctorShrink_directSum {ι : Type} [Finite ι] (g : ι → A)
    (N : ι → ModuleCat.{w} A) (W : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{w} A))
    (hW : ∀ j, IsZero ((locDerivedShrink.{w} (g j)).obj W))
    (hN : ∀ j, IsUnit (algebraMap A (Module.End A (N j)) (g j))) (q : ℤ) :
    Subsingleton (W ⟶ (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} A) q).obj
      (ModuleCat.of A (DirectSum ι (fun j => (N j : Type w))))) := by
  classical
  have : Fintype ι := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  have e₁ : ModuleCat.of A (DirectSum ι (fun j => (N j : Type w))) ≅ ∏ᶜ N :=
    (DirectSum.linearEquivFunOnFintype A ι (fun j => (N j : Type w))).toModuleIso ≪≫
      (ModuleCat.piIsoPi N).symm
  refine subsingleton_hom_of_iso
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} A) q).mapIso e₁).symm ?_
  refine subsingleton_hom_of_iso
    (PreservesProduct.iso (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} A) q) N).symm ?_
  exact subsingleton_hom_pi W _ fun j =>
    subsingleton_hom_singleFunctorShrink_of_isUnit_smul.{w} (g j) W (hW j) (N j) (hN j) q

/-! ### The Čech terms are invisible to torsion objects, at a free module universe

This is where the small model of the Čech complex and the small model of the localization
functor meet. `Stacks.LocalCohomology.subsingleton_hom_singleFunctor_extendedCechComplex_X`
needs both at once — the terms of the complex and the derived localizations detecting power
torsion — so it is pinned at `ModuleCat.{max u v}` even though neither ingredient has to be. -/

section CechTerms

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → R)
  (M : Type w') [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Small.{w} M]

/-- The degree-`p` term of the small Čech complex is the direct sum of the small models of the
Čech localizations, as an object of `ModuleCat.{w} R`. Stated as a definition closed by
`Iso.refl` rather than as a `simp` lemma: an equation between the projection `(K.X p)` and a
`ModuleCat.of` rewrites inside types. -/
def cechComplexShrinkXAsDirectSum (p : ℕ) :
    (Cech.cechComplexShrink.{w} f M).X p ≅
      ModuleCat.of R (DirectSum {s : Finset (Fin r) // s.card = p}
        fun s => (Cech.cechModCatShrink.{w} f M s.1 : Type w)) :=
  Iso.refl _

/-- In degree `p : ℕ` the integer-indexed small Čech complex is the small Čech complex. -/
private def extendedCechComplexShrinkXIso (p : ℕ) :
    (Cech.extendedCechComplexShrink.{w} f M).X p ≅ (Cech.cechComplexShrink.{w} f M).X p :=
  HomologicalComplex.extendXIso (Cech.cechComplexShrink.{w} f M)
    ComplexShape.embeddingUpNat (i := p) (i' := (p : ℤ)) (by simp)

/-- Above degree `r` the integer-indexed small Čech complex vanishes. -/
theorem isZero_extendedCechComplexShrink_X_of_gt {i : ℤ} (hi : (r : ℤ) < i) :
    IsZero ((Cech.extendedCechComplexShrink.{w} f M).X i) := by
  by_cases h0 : 0 ≤ i
  · obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ : ∃ p : ℕ, i = (p : ℤ) := ⟨i.toNat, by omega⟩
    refine IsZero.of_iso ?_ (extendedCechComplexShrinkXIso.{w} f M p)
    rw [ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton]
    exact Cech.subsingleton_cechTermShrink_of_lt.{w} f M (by exact_mod_cast hi)
  · exact Cech.isZero_extendedCechComplexShrink_X_of_neg.{w} f M (by omega)

/-- **The Čech terms away from degree zero are invisible to torsion objects, in a module
universe independent of the ring universe.** A complex with `I`-power-torsion cohomology admits
no nonzero morphism to any term of the small Čech complex other than the degree-zero one, placed
in any degree. This is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.subsingleton_hom_singleFunctor_extendedCechComplex_X` with the
constraint `ModuleCat.{max u v}` removed; it consumes the small Čech complex of
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.Shrink` and the small derived localization above, which is why it is
stated here rather than in either of them. -/
theorem subsingleton_hom_singleFunctorShrink_extendedCechComplexShrink_X
    (I : Ideal R) (hI : I.FG) (hIf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I)
    (W : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{w} R))
    (hW : Dualizing.derivedPowerTorsionProperty R I hI W) (i : ℤ) (hi : i ≠ 0) (q : ℤ) :
    Subsingleton (W ⟶ (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} R) q).obj
      ((Cech.extendedCechComplexShrink.{w} f M).X i)) := by
  classical
  by_cases hout : i < 0 ∨ (r : ℤ) < i
  · have hz := (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} R) q).map_isZero
      (hout.elim (Cech.isZero_extendedCechComplexShrink_X_of_neg.{w} f M)
        (isZero_extendedCechComplexShrink_X_of_gt.{w} f M))
    exact ⟨hz.eq_of_tgt⟩
  · obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ : ∃ p : ℕ, i = (p : ℤ) := ⟨i.toNat, by omega⟩
    have hp : 0 < p := by omega
    have hgen : Ideal.span ((Finset.image f Finset.univ : Finset R) : Set R) = I := by
      rw [← hIf, Finset.coe_image, Finset.coe_univ, Set.image_univ]
    have hWloc := (Dualizing.derivedPowerTorsionProperty_iff_isZero_mapDerivedCategory
      I hI _ hgen W).mp hW
    have hne : ∀ s : {s : Finset (Fin r) // s.card = p}, s.1.Nonempty := fun s =>
      Finset.card_pos.mp (s.2.symm ▸ hp)
    refine subsingleton_hom_of_iso
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} R) q).mapIso
        (extendedCechComplexShrinkXIso.{w} f M p).symm) ?_
    refine subsingleton_hom_of_iso
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} R) q).mapIso
        (cechComplexShrinkXAsDirectSum.{w} f M p).symm) ?_
    refine subsingleton_hom_singleFunctorShrink_directSum.{w}
      (fun s : {s : Finset (Fin r) // s.card = p} => f (hne s).choose)
      (fun s => Cech.cechModCatShrink.{w} f M s.1) W (fun s => ?_) (fun s => ?_) q
    · exact hWloc _ (Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨(hne s).choose, Finset.mem_univ _, rfl⟩)
    · exact Cech.isUnit_algebraMap_cechModCatShrink.{w} f M (hne s).choose_spec

end CechTerms

